WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.880
You've gotta be fast on your feet to keep up with Nintendo soccer!

00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:26.020
And welcome to NEStalgia, a chronological exploration of every NES game played in North America.

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:27.100
I'm Mike.

00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:28.760
I'm Sean. I'm Sam.

00:00:28.760 --> 00:00:29.740
I'm Joe.

00:00:30.380 --> 00:00:32.940
Joe, welcome again from...

00:00:32.940 --> 00:00:33.820
Tel Aviv.

00:00:34.060 --> 00:00:35.100
Tel Aviv!

00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:36.380
That's where I am.

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:38.100
Sean always knows. How's the weather down there?

00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:40.080
It's good. It's great.

00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:41.200
What do I usually say? It's great.

00:00:41.620 --> 00:00:44.340
Yeah, it's great. Joe, have you ever ran into Carmen Sandiego?

00:00:45.080 --> 00:00:46.140
That's what I'm looking for.

00:00:47.340 --> 00:00:48.800
That makes a lot of sense.

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:51.340
That would kill Sean for some reason.

00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:55.440
That's good. As long as someone laughs at my bad jokes.

00:00:55.440 --> 00:01:01.140
Yeah, I'll tell you though, since you're traveling, it's appropriate that we only play Nintendo

00:01:01.140 --> 00:01:06.240
Soccer, otherwise just known as Soccer for the NES, because that has countries from all

00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:07.060
over the world in it.

00:01:07.220 --> 00:01:08.120
All over. Right.

00:01:08.120 --> 00:01:11.460
It's everywhere. It's places such as the United States.

00:01:12.220 --> 00:01:13.740
Yeah. Uh...

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:15.560
What are you pointing at me?

00:01:15.580 --> 00:01:17.140
The Free Republic of Germany.

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:19.700
Yeah, yeah, yeah. It's got West Germany in it.

00:01:19.760 --> 00:01:21.180
West Germany is in this game.

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:26.860
Um, and this game was made by Intelligent Systems, uh, which probably means nothing to

00:01:26.860 --> 00:01:30.300
most people. To be honest, I'm a little worried if it actually is made by them.

00:01:30.300 --> 00:01:33.820
Um, but I did a lot of research for this and it's listed on their website, but they swear

00:01:33.820 --> 00:01:36.460
this game was made in 1986, which is impossible.

00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:41.640
The copyright says 1985, but Intelligent Systems swears they made this game in 86.

00:01:42.100 --> 00:01:45.700
But the reason why I even bring them up is because they're a big deal for Nintendo.

00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:48.820
Uh, they're kind of like a second party developer for Nintendo.

00:01:49.020 --> 00:01:53.260
They've made other games too, but they're responsible for the Fire Emblem series, the

00:01:53.260 --> 00:01:56.180
Advanced Wars series, and the Paper Mario series.

00:01:56.180 --> 00:02:00.380
So that's like three really solid series, even though unfortunately we haven't really

00:02:00.380 --> 00:02:05.180
seen a great Paper Mario or a, uh, we haven't even seen an Advanced Wars in a while.

00:02:05.460 --> 00:02:07.060
I'd just like to see that in general.

00:02:07.400 --> 00:02:09.800
But that's, that's for a different kind of podcast.

00:02:09.820 --> 00:02:10.940
It's a great pedigree. Yep.

00:02:11.140 --> 00:02:12.780
Today we're talking about soccer.

00:02:13.160 --> 00:02:18.260
Um, the game that people play in real life and, uh, you can also play on your NES.

00:02:18.260 --> 00:02:19.440
So let's get some impressions.

00:02:33.740 --> 00:02:34.900
Uh, yeah.

00:02:34.980 --> 00:02:38.560
So my first impression with soccer was calm down soccer.

00:02:38.700 --> 00:02:42.780
The music at this initial screen is like I'm at a carnival or something.

00:02:42.780 --> 00:02:48.040
And I think Mike, I think it was you that said that you wanted some music, uh, during

00:02:48.040 --> 00:02:49.420
baseball or during 10 yard fight.

00:02:49.540 --> 00:02:50.800
That was absolutely me.

00:02:50.980 --> 00:02:57.060
You got your wish because there is, there's definitely some, just some loud, crazy music

00:02:57.060 --> 00:02:58.300
going on through this whole game.

00:02:58.720 --> 00:03:02.080
Um, but also it, it, the game played like soccer.

00:03:02.560 --> 00:03:05.120
I wasn't crazy about it, but I wasn't upset with it.

00:03:05.360 --> 00:03:06.440
That was my initial impression.

00:03:06.960 --> 00:03:08.460
All right, Sean. Sean. Okay.

00:03:08.660 --> 00:03:16.620
Yeah. Um, the ridiculous nonstop backing music of this game, notwithstanding, I kind of like

00:03:16.620 --> 00:03:22.340
soccer. And again, I'm the resident sports fan, uh, sports fan sports game fan.

00:03:22.620 --> 00:03:24.400
Um, I had a lot of fun with soccer.

00:03:24.600 --> 00:03:33.060
Um, I think it was, uh, the best representation of a physical sport, um, so far that we've played.

00:03:33.520 --> 00:03:37.580
Um, maybe, maybe baseball's up there too, but you can't really feel, but like, I'm

00:03:37.580 --> 00:03:45.000
like, um, I really liked all of the creative solutions to, um, how to represent certain

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:49.680
things in between passing, shooting, aiming, and all that fun stuff, dribbling.

00:03:49.860 --> 00:03:51.300
Um, I really liked it.

00:03:51.520 --> 00:03:53.100
Um, I don't know if y'all agree.

00:03:53.280 --> 00:04:00.020
Thank goodness. You said physical sport because I was like how quickly we forgot golf, but not a physical

00:04:00.020 --> 00:04:01.640
sport. So I'll allow it.

00:04:01.740 --> 00:04:03.660
You know, you're talking about contact sports or whatever.

00:04:03.660 --> 00:04:08.580
Uh, and my initial impression was I was happy with more options.

00:04:08.800 --> 00:04:12.200
I thought that was kind of cool that you can actually choose a skill level, uh, something

00:04:12.200 --> 00:04:15.700
we couldn't do in baseball or something we couldn't really do in 10 yard fight because

00:04:15.700 --> 00:04:19.080
there was no difference between high school and super bowl really.

00:04:19.680 --> 00:04:23.440
Um, and I also liked, uh, the ability to choose time too.

00:04:23.580 --> 00:04:27.380
That was kind of cool. It's just way it was like, okay, I want to play a fast game or, you know, like there's

00:04:27.380 --> 00:04:28.960
going to be an epic duel between me and my friend.

00:04:29.500 --> 00:04:34.720
Once I actually started playing the game, my initial impression soured pretty fast.

00:04:34.880 --> 00:04:37.000
I don't know if soccer is just not for me.

00:04:37.200 --> 00:04:39.600
Full disclosure. I didn't grow up with any soccer.

00:04:39.900 --> 00:04:41.620
My, my dad was not a soccer guy.

00:04:41.700 --> 00:04:42.620
We never watched any.

00:04:42.740 --> 00:04:48.340
I never really played any, but, um, I understand the rules and I just felt like ball handling

00:04:48.340 --> 00:04:52.500
in this game in general, it's, it's, it's rough and I get it.

00:04:52.500 --> 00:04:53.880
It's an NES launch game.

00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:58.580
It has some limitations, but this is a little rougher than I expected it to be when I compared

00:04:58.580 --> 00:05:03.640
to, um, you know, how fluid the passing was even in 10 yard fight.

00:05:03.960 --> 00:05:07.880
Uh, granted there was an easy chance for an interception cause there was no Z axis, but

00:05:07.880 --> 00:05:09.500
the past, which thankfully is in this game.

00:05:09.660 --> 00:05:11.520
Yeah. I wasn't impressed with that too.

00:05:12.280 --> 00:05:13.940
Uh, which I can't say so much here.

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:16.000
So my initial impression, not that great, Sam.

00:05:16.200 --> 00:05:18.840
Yeah. Um, I'm kind of on the same page as Sean.

00:05:19.180 --> 00:05:22.480
I think I, I've had a really nice little time with this one.

00:05:22.480 --> 00:05:29.560
I thought that it felt the most like, uh, like my actions were controlling the game,

00:05:29.860 --> 00:05:33.760
you know, which in a lot of the other sports games, I feel it didn't.

00:05:34.140 --> 00:05:39.340
Um, I think that they, they got down a lot of different things.

00:05:39.500 --> 00:05:42.960
You know, I feel like just the, the basic mechanics were pretty solid.

00:05:43.300 --> 00:05:47.200
And after that, it was pretty, it was pretty simple.

00:05:47.500 --> 00:05:51.780
You know, if anything, I would say it might be, it might be, well, I played on the easy

00:05:51.780 --> 00:05:55.660
level. So it might be too easy on the easy level, which makes sense.

00:05:55.940 --> 00:05:57.740
I felt just to chime in for a second.

00:05:57.940 --> 00:05:59.900
I did feel like easy was too easy.

00:06:00.040 --> 00:06:02.900
Yeah. I was up four goals before the second half.

00:06:03.020 --> 00:06:07.000
Yeah. You can just kind of dribble at the goal and then shoot it at the goal and then you score.

00:06:07.360 --> 00:06:10.500
Uh, but I thought it, it felt really solid.

00:06:16.200 --> 00:06:22.660
I think the, uh, there is a, there's a difficulty progression between which, um, which setting

00:06:22.660 --> 00:06:24.520
you use, which is nice to see.

00:06:24.600 --> 00:06:29.640
And it, it actually like, it's one that you feel unlike, uh, like we said, 10 yard fight,

00:06:29.780 --> 00:06:30.900
you can't really tell the difference.

00:06:30.900 --> 00:06:35.780
Um, and yeah, like I jumped up from one to two.

00:06:36.060 --> 00:06:37.180
It was still a little easy.

00:06:37.360 --> 00:06:39.080
You got to three. It felt pretty good.

00:06:39.220 --> 00:06:40.760
I tried four and they beat me.

00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:44.620
So, um, I was, I was really impressed with this game.

00:06:44.620 --> 00:06:50.640
I think that the rhythm of like just getting in the rhythm of running and dribbling and

00:06:50.640 --> 00:06:53.120
trying to like deke your opponent out.

00:06:53.540 --> 00:06:57.920
I know that Mike had a lot of problems, not problems, but you, you, you weren't a big

00:06:57.920 --> 00:06:59.700
fan of how the controls felt.

00:06:59.780 --> 00:07:01.020
Felt a little clunky. Yeah.

00:07:01.260 --> 00:07:08.040
I thought they felt pretty good and just because soccer is a very stop and go.

00:07:08.680 --> 00:07:13.680
Um, at least in the video game representations, cause you, you're always trying to catch up

00:07:13.680 --> 00:07:14.600
to the ball. He just kicked.

00:07:15.140 --> 00:07:17.120
Um, so I appreciate it.

00:07:17.200 --> 00:07:19.900
I don't know if, if Sam or Joe feel that way at all.

00:07:19.900 --> 00:07:24.700
Yeah. I thought that it looked clunky, but once you realize why, you know, like when you turn

00:07:24.700 --> 00:07:30.200
and the ball turns with you, that's, that, that's just kind of the way, the best way.

00:07:30.340 --> 00:07:34.920
I think that they could illustrate what's happening, but like, yeah, when a soccer player turns

00:07:34.920 --> 00:07:36.940
and they have the ball, like they don't have, you know what I mean?

00:07:36.980 --> 00:07:38.740
Like they can turn relatively easily.

00:07:38.980 --> 00:07:41.880
It's not what it's going to look like the way it looked like in this NES game.

00:07:41.880 --> 00:07:44.840
But once you kind of get past that, I think it felt good.

00:07:44.840 --> 00:07:45.900
It just looked clunky.

00:07:46.080 --> 00:07:51.320
The one clunky thing, uh, at least with the controls that I will seed, um, was the fact

00:07:51.320 --> 00:07:56.520
that like, if you're controlling one of your defensemen and you're getting run up on, you

00:07:56.520 --> 00:08:02.400
gotta be careful because not only are you controlling like your last defenseman, you're also controlling

00:08:02.400 --> 00:08:05.140
your goalie, which screwed me up so much.

00:08:05.240 --> 00:08:06.740
Like just the first time.

00:08:06.840 --> 00:08:09.360
Like I was like, wow, I am not even near the net right now.

00:08:09.360 --> 00:08:13.780
Like panic. There were a few times where I, I lost my goalie cause I was looking at my defensemen.

00:08:13.880 --> 00:08:15.820
Exactly. Where'd my goalie go?

00:08:16.400 --> 00:08:19.940
Once they get inside the box, that's when it changes your controls over.

00:08:20.520 --> 00:08:21.800
Right, right. That's in the manual.

00:08:22.340 --> 00:08:25.080
You are controlling, uh, both at once.

00:08:25.280 --> 00:08:26.200
Really? I believe so.

00:08:26.200 --> 00:08:32.240
Yeah. Okay. And, uh, it's also sort of the way that when you're on the attack, you're not only are

00:08:32.240 --> 00:08:38.140
you, are you moving more towards the goal or setting up your play, but every time you press

00:08:38.140 --> 00:08:42.860
up or down, you're also aiming your shot and it's sort of, it, it, it, it crosses over

00:08:42.860 --> 00:08:48.460
so that it's possible to go from one corner to the other immediately and kind of, uh, get

00:08:48.460 --> 00:08:50.340
the goalie, you know, in a weird position.

00:08:50.600 --> 00:08:54.540
Um, I thought, I thought these are really interesting ways to solve these problems.

00:08:55.000 --> 00:08:57.420
Um, they didn't always work the best.

00:08:57.880 --> 00:09:00.320
Um, but I give them an A for effort.

00:09:00.640 --> 00:09:07.380
Yeah. I think, uh, what I, I wanted to add the, uh, one of my favorite parts of the game was

00:09:07.380 --> 00:09:10.820
when you score, your guys just go nuts.

00:09:11.020 --> 00:09:12.280
They go nuts. And I love that.

00:09:12.420 --> 00:09:13.780
The celebration is so cool.

00:09:13.920 --> 00:09:15.380
The animations are so funny.

00:09:15.520 --> 00:09:17.580
They're like, well, they're flapping their arms and everything.

00:09:17.580 --> 00:09:18.700
It was great.

00:09:19.080 --> 00:09:22.160
Is that, I don't even know what they're trying to simulate when they're flapping.

00:09:22.240 --> 00:09:26.360
It's like, they're trying to look like birds or like the guy who scores does something

00:09:26.360 --> 00:09:27.460
a little bit different too.

00:09:27.640 --> 00:09:29.180
And it's just, I don't know.

00:09:29.280 --> 00:09:31.700
It was just, it was really, it was a joy.

00:09:32.340 --> 00:09:36.200
I would love to see a real soccer game in which they do that whenever they score.

00:09:36.380 --> 00:09:39.920
I just kind of felt like, uh, you know, at any moment, the guy who scored was just

00:09:39.920 --> 00:09:45.020
going to like slide on his knees, you know, like take his shirt off and be like, Oh my

00:09:45.020 --> 00:09:47.680
God. Like, and there's a halftime show.

00:09:47.800 --> 00:09:49.360
Yeah. Can we get to the halftime show?

00:09:49.420 --> 00:09:50.480
Because. I love that.

00:09:59.980 --> 00:10:04.000
First of all, I'm not sure if that happens in soccer.

00:10:04.280 --> 00:10:05.080
Not that I know.

00:10:05.080 --> 00:10:06.360
I don't watch a lot of soccer.

00:10:06.460 --> 00:10:11.220
I've watched some, but even if there is like a halftime show, is it really just cheerleaders

00:10:11.220 --> 00:10:12.560
that come out? Right.

00:10:12.960 --> 00:10:14.120
I can't even think about it.

00:10:14.780 --> 00:10:19.540
What I think is funny is that, I mean, the purpose of a halftime show is to like entertain

00:10:19.540 --> 00:10:22.180
you while the game's not happening, but this is a video game.

00:10:22.180 --> 00:10:24.600
You could just, the game could just start happening again.

00:10:24.760 --> 00:10:29.140
I mean, I don't even know if you can skip it, but if you really miss a treat because like

00:10:29.140 --> 00:10:32.380
these, these sprites are so poorly rendered.

00:10:32.380 --> 00:10:35.440
I mean, like they, they look great.

00:10:35.600 --> 00:10:36.520
I mean, I don't think they look great.

00:10:36.620 --> 00:10:42.440
They look fine on the field as players, but like these, these cheerleaders look like the

00:10:42.440 --> 00:10:43.260
scene in E.T.

00:10:43.960 --> 00:10:46.340
where it puts the dress and wig on.

00:10:47.300 --> 00:10:50.180
I didn't understand what they were going for with this.

00:10:50.180 --> 00:10:53.800
Like just the shape of the head doesn't match the shape of the player's head.

00:10:53.860 --> 00:10:56.020
The heads are very round on the cheerleaders.

00:10:56.220 --> 00:10:57.540
They're very like oval shaped.

00:10:57.840 --> 00:10:59.300
It was an odd decision.

00:10:59.580 --> 00:11:01.680
I mean, but you know, character for the game.

00:11:01.820 --> 00:11:05.060
Yeah. I actually kind of love the halftime show.

00:11:05.180 --> 00:11:08.920
It cracks me up, but this is maximal soccer, right?

00:11:10.340 --> 00:11:17.100
Uh, and also speaking of the sprites, I noticed that the, the goalie's sprite, his shirt and

00:11:17.100 --> 00:11:18.500
his hair are reversed.

00:11:18.500 --> 00:11:23.240
So if he had a red shirt, he'll have red hair and whatever color his hair was is his shirt

00:11:23.240 --> 00:11:25.900
color. So I know that that's, I mean like technical answer.

00:11:25.960 --> 00:11:31.540
That's a color limitation of the, but no, no, like it needed to be that way for the amount

00:11:31.540 --> 00:11:35.800
of like different colors that you can fit in a, in a section of sprites.

00:11:36.260 --> 00:11:38.980
Uh, but like, no, that's like a cool workaround.

00:11:39.160 --> 00:11:40.420
No, I think that's a cool workaround.

00:11:40.600 --> 00:11:46.300
Yeah. And also it's also appropriate for the game because it, when you're watching soccer, the

00:11:46.300 --> 00:11:51.800
goaltender or the goalkeeper will usually be wearing a different Jersey just for everyone's

00:11:51.800 --> 00:11:55.000
like, right. Just make sure everyone isn't confused as to who's who.

00:11:55.400 --> 00:11:59.160
But could you not have just recolored the Jersey and left the hair?

00:11:59.400 --> 00:12:04.240
So it didn't, so people didn't have blue colored hair or that's kind of, that's what

00:12:04.240 --> 00:12:09.220
Mike's saying. I think that they didn't want to have the hair and the Jersey be the same exact color.

00:12:09.620 --> 00:12:10.560
Right. Yeah.

00:12:10.640 --> 00:12:16.100
That makes sense. Yeah. Uh, so since we're on the topic of the goalies though, I just wanted to talk about what I

00:12:16.100 --> 00:12:17.920
think is the best aspect of this game.

00:12:17.920 --> 00:12:20.060
And that's the shooting the goal.

00:12:20.420 --> 00:12:24.840
Like it's very intuitive, uh, as opposed to the passing, which I felt was kind of like,

00:12:25.120 --> 00:12:28.660
yes, you can control it a little bit, but I felt like nine times out of 10, if I'm passing

00:12:28.660 --> 00:12:30.560
that ball, it's like, good luck.

00:12:30.740 --> 00:12:35.220
Yeah. It was a very rudimentary version of like in FIFA.

00:12:35.280 --> 00:12:40.340
You could just like press the analog stick in a direction and it'll say like this, this

00:12:40.340 --> 00:12:43.280
is probably the player trying to pass to and it'll go there.

00:12:43.460 --> 00:12:48.620
Whereas in this one, you kind of cycle through highlighted characters or highlighted players.

00:12:48.900 --> 00:12:52.040
And I mean, it, it was a good idea.

00:12:52.340 --> 00:12:55.480
It wasn't the best execution, but it was an execution.

00:12:55.480 --> 00:12:56.560
It was an execution.

00:12:56.560 --> 00:13:01.960
It was, it was 99 times out of the 10, like if you, if you played enough of the game, you'll

00:13:01.960 --> 00:13:03.680
get, you'll pass to the correct player.

00:13:04.240 --> 00:13:08.080
Um, but yeah, the shooting is definitely more intuitive than the passing.

00:13:08.720 --> 00:13:12.940
Um, just because I like, I like that arrow, you know, like the ability to kind of say like,

00:13:13.120 --> 00:13:15.260
this is where I'm going to shoot and stuff like that.

00:13:15.580 --> 00:13:19.880
And having some control over that kind of brings me back to like with golf where you

00:13:19.880 --> 00:13:22.740
had the power meter and it's like give control over your swing.

00:13:22.840 --> 00:13:24.520
It's not just like, yeah, all right, here I go.

00:13:24.600 --> 00:13:25.760
I'm about to take a big swing.

00:13:25.760 --> 00:13:28.640
You know, it's like, I can control how much I want to take of this swing.

00:13:28.840 --> 00:13:33.240
Similar to how, like what we wished in baseball or football, if you could say like, I want

00:13:33.240 --> 00:13:37.100
to throw to this guy in football or in baseball, I want to swing this hard.

00:13:37.100 --> 00:13:43.920
Like, uh, the, the one part that, uh, it kind of is counterintuitive is it really telegraphs.

00:13:44.000 --> 00:13:47.340
If you're playing two players, it really telegraphs where you're going to shoot the ball.

00:13:47.600 --> 00:13:54.120
Um, but I think that a workaround is the fact that, um, where you're shooting isn't really

00:13:54.120 --> 00:14:01.640
bounded. If you hit the top corner or if you move towards the top corner and you keep going, you will go

00:14:01.640 --> 00:14:05.160
back to the bottom corner and maybe throw, throw your, uh, your opponent on.

00:14:11.960 --> 00:14:16.700
Speaking of multiplayer, I think personally, that's, that's where I find the most enjoyment

00:14:16.700 --> 00:14:19.900
out of this game as someone who, I'm not a big, you know, sports game fan anyways.

00:14:19.900 --> 00:14:21.940
So I would just rather be competing with someone.

00:14:22.260 --> 00:14:26.920
So I kind of just went to, I played one, one match against the computer on easy mode.

00:14:26.920 --> 00:14:30.820
And then I just went straight to playing against another real player, which I found more fun.

00:14:30.980 --> 00:14:32.420
Yeah. You have so many friends, Joe.

